WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:06.190
Radon is in the same group as helium and the
other noble gases. It’s in

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:12.750
the highly un-reactive material. However radon
has quite an importance

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:18.689
because it is formed by the radioactive decomposition
of some other

00:00:18.689 --> 00:00:25.359
elements. As I mentioned you can imagine radioactivity
as a droplet of

00:00:25.359 --> 00:00:31.769
water splitting into two, and they don’t
have to split into equal halves and

00:00:31.769 --> 00:00:37.940
you can quite often be left with radon. Now
if you live in areas of the

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:43.890
world where there is radioactive material
in the minerals in the ground,

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:48.750
then radon as a gas, which is quite long-lived,
can come up through the

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:54.001
ground and accumulate in your house, and then
if you breathe it in, in

00:00:54.001 --> 00:00:58.930
principle it can cause lung cancer, and so
there are some parts of the UK

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:02.269
where radon levels are much higher than others
particularly those areas

00:01:02.269 --> 00:01:06.950
that are based on granite. But it’s very
unpredictable because if there

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.950
happens to be cracks in the rocks under your
house you can get more

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:15.439
radon than the guy next door and so there
has, from time to time, been

00:01:15.439 --> 00:01:20.970
a lot of worry about radon in the air. But
for most people it’s not

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:22.631
something that you should really worry about.

